{#- The search page.

    The overlay in partials/search.njk is a JS-only control: it is
    `display:none` until js/ui.js adds `open`, so with script off it can never
    appear and the header's search control was a button that did nothing. The
    control is now a real link to this page, and ui.js intercepts the click
    when script is available.

    This page carries the same destinations the overlay's `.so-links` block
    lists, as ordinary page markup that renders with script off.

    CONTENT: destinations from _data/chrome.json (searchShortcuts) plus the
    Receipts link the overlay lists first — the same list, the same labels.
    Nothing here is new copy.

    DESIGN: `.titleband` / `.breadcrumb` follow accessibility.njk; the
    destinations use the export's own `.btn-row` + `.u-btn` pattern (see
    about.njk), so this page needs no new CSS. -#}
<header class="titleband">
  <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Uncost</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp; <span>Search</span></div>
  <h1>Search</h1>
</header>
<section class="blk" data-screen-label="Search">
  <div class="btn-row">
    <a href="/receipts/" class="u-btn u-btn--ghost">Search the Receipts</a>
    {%- for link in chrome.searchShortcuts %}
    <a href="{{ link.url }}" class="u-btn u-btn--ghost">{{ link.label }}</a>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</section>
